
---
import DocsLayout from '/src/layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import DocsCode from '/src/components/DocsCode.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Lua & LSL Docs">
<div class="dashboard summary-constant">
  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`VEHICLE_FLAG_HOVER_TERRAIN_ONLY: number = 8`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`integer VEHICLE_FLAG_HOVER_TERRAIN_ONLY = 8;`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>The integer constant VEHICLE_FLAG_HOVER_TERRAIN_ONLY has the value 0x008</p>
  <p>Makes the vehicle float over land.</p>
  <p>If you wanted to make a boat you should set the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/VEHICLE_FLAG_HOVER_WATER_ONLY" target="_blank">VEHICLE_FLAG_HOVER_WATER_ONLY</a> flag, or if you wanted to drive a hover tank under water you would use the VEHICLE_FLAG_HOVER_TERRAIN_ONLY flag instead. Finally, if you wanted to make a submarine or a balloon you would use the <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/VEHICLE_FLAG_HOVER_GLOBAL_HEIGHT" target="_blank">VEHICLE_FLAG_HOVER_GLOBAL_HEIGHT</a>.</p>
  <p>The vehicle flags are independent of each other and that setting two contradictory flags will have undefined behavior. The flags are set using the script call <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlSetVehicleFlags" target="_blank">llSetVehicleFlags</a>.</p>
</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Member Of</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>VehicleFlag</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>

      <div class="label-stack">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
